he rehabilitation of timber structures (in Italian). Libreria Tecnica Hoepli, Milan, Italy"},{"key":"9650_CR35","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","DOI":"10.1142\/p055","volume-title":"Earthquake-resistant design of masonry buildings","author":"M Toma\u017eevic","year":"1999","unstructured":"Toma\u017eevic M (1999) Earthquake-resistant design of masonry buildings. Imperial College Press, London"},{"issue":"9","key":"9650_CR36","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1040","DOI":"10.1061\/(ASCE)0733-9445(1996)122:9(1040)","volume":"122","author":"M Toma\u017eevi\u010d","year":"1996","unstructured":"Toma\u017eevi\u010d M, Lutman M, Petkovi\u010d L (1996) Seismic behaviour of masonry walls: experimental simulation. J Struct Eng 122(9):1040\u20131047","journal-title":"J Struct Eng"},{"key":"9650_CR37","unstructured":"Tsakanika-Theohari E (2006) The structural role of timber in palatial architecture of Minoan Crete (in Greek). Ph.D. Thesis, National Technical University of Athens (NTUA)"},{"issue":"10","key":"9650_CR38","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1269","DOI":"10.1061\/(ASCE)ST.1943-541X.0000053","volume":"135","author":"G Vasconcelos","year":"2009","unstructured":"Vasconcelos G, Louren\u00e7o PB (2009) In-plane experimental behavior of stone masonry walls under cyclic loading. J Struct Eng 135(10):1269\u20131277","journal-title":"J Struct Eng"},{"key":"9650_CR39","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1028","DOI":"10.1016\/j.engstruct.2013.05.017","volume":"56","author":"G Vasconcelos","year":"2013","unstructured":"Vasconcelos G, Poletti E, Salavessa E, Jesus A, Louren\u00e7o P, Pilaon P (2013) In-plane shear behaviour of traditional timber walls. Eng Struct 56:1028\u20131048","journal-title":"Eng Struct"},{"key":"9650_CR40","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"102","DOI":"10.1016\/j.engstruct.2014.02.020","volume":"69","author":"F Vieux-Champagne","year":"2014","unstructured":"Vieux-Champagne F, Sieffert Y, Grange S, Polastri A, Ceccotti A, Daudeville L (2014) Experimental analysis of seismic resistance of timber-framed structures with stones and earth infill. Eng Struct 69:102\u2013115","journal-title":"Eng Struct"},{"key":"9650_CR41","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"225","DOI":"10.1016\/j.conbuildmat.2005.04.002","volume":"21","author":"E Vintzileou","year":"2007","unstructured":"Vintzileou E, Zagkotsis A, Repapis C, Zeris Ch (2007) Seismic behaviour of the historical structural system of the island of Lefkada, Greece. Constr Build Mat 21:225\u2013236","journal-title":"Constr Build Mat"}],"container-title":["Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/link.springer.com\/content\/pdf\/10.1007\/s10518-014-9650-9.pdf","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"http:\/\/link.springer.com\/article\/10.1007\/s10518-014-9650-9\/fulltext.html","content-type":"text\/html","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"http:\/\/link.springer.com\/content\/pdf\/10.1007\/s10518-014-9650-9","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2019,5,29]],"date-time":"2019-05-29T19:41:15Z","timestamp":1559158875000},"score":29.968037,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/link.springer.com\/10.1007\/s10518-014-9650-9"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2014,7,2]]},"references-count":41,"journal-issue":{"issue":"3","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2015,3]]}},"alternative-id":["9650"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/s10518-014-9650-9","ISSN":["1570-761X","1573-1456"],"issn-type":[{"value":"1570-761X","type":"print"},{"value":"1573-1456","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2014,7,2]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,17]],"date-time":"2025-12-17T13:07:28Z","timestamp":1765976848534,"version":"3.40.4"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"University of Zagreb Faculty of Civil Engineering","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>The recent earthquakes in Croatia have reminded us that heritage masonry buildings are highly vulnerable to seismic actions. This paper will focus on the out-of-plane failure mechanisms, which result from scarce wall-to-wall and wall-to-floor connections. To prevent these mechanisms, masonry buildings should have adequate structural integrity, i.e. they should behave like a box. \nThis paper examines the use of ties in an 18th century stone masonry building in Krk, Croatia. Over the years, the three-story building has undergone various reconstructions. The floor structures are made of timber beams and boards, as is common in this region. The beneficial connecting details include: i) the connection between the timber beams and the masonry walls made via anchoring iron ties, placed at every third beam in the floor; ii) the attic walls connected via iron ties at corners to prevent their separation; iii) diagonal iron ties used to connect the attic walls and the floor beams and iv) timber ring beams inserted into the walls to act as a horizontal tie. Although the use of timber ring beams as ties is quite common in adobe masonry, it is not so common in stone masonry. The authors have not so far detected any timber ring beams embedded into masonry in this region. The mechanical properties of wrought iron ties have also been investigated.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.5592\/co\/3crocee.2025.114","type":"proceedings-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,4,24]],"date-time":"2025-04-24T13:05:55Z","timestamp":1745499955000},"page":"380-389","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["TIES IN UNREINFORCED MASONRY STRUCTURES: CASE STUDY IN KRK"],"prefix":"10.5592","volume":"3","author":[{"given":"Paulo","family":"\u0160\u0107ulac","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Kristina","family":"Galjani\u0107","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Davor","family":"Grandi\u0107","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Josipa","family":"Mihaljevi\u0107","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"\u017deljko","family":"Smol\u010di\u0107","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"3653","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,19]]},"event":{"name":"3rd Croatian Conference on Earthquake Engineering","acronym":"3CROCEE"},"container-title":["Conference proceedings (Croatian Conference on Earthquake Engineering)","3rd Croatian Conference on Earthquake Engineering - 3CroCEE"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/crocee.grad.hr\/event\/3\/contributions\/439\/attachments\/406\/546\/3CroCEE_114.pdf","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,4,24]],"date-time":"2025-04-24T13:05:57Z","timestamp":1745499957000},"score":28.544844,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/crocee.grad.hr\/event\/3\/contributions\/439\/"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,19]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5592\/co\/3crocee.2025.114","ISSN":["3043-8071"],"issn-type":[{"value":"3043-8071","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,19]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,23]],"date-time":"2026-10-23T23:46:33Z","timestamp":1792799193150,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":38,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2015,10,1]],"date-time":"2015-10-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1443657600000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/www.elsevier.com\/tdm\/userlicense\/1.0\/"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2015,10,1]],"date-time":"2015-10-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1443657600000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/www.elsevier.com\/legal\/tdmrep-license"}],"conten